{"event_id": "evt_0017", "session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sandbox c, night", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for amw8gtiazcaiqib.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": [], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "The blaster goes back in its holster. You cross to the cart, shrug the pack round, and fish the coil of syntherope out left-handed while the blade hums in your right, held well away from the rope.\n\nIt is slow work. Torch and hose first, then the two bottles back to back, cold steel against your knuckles. You hold the hilt out at arm's length and pull the knots tight with your left hand, your teeth, the crook of your elbow. Three minutes, maybe. The rope crosses over both shoulders and bites in at your waist. When you straighten, the load settles high on your back and stays there.\n\nIt is heavy. Every step back toward the shed the bottles knock together, a dull bell in the quiet.\n\nYou stand at the chained door again, the blade lit in your right hand, your left hand free, the weight on your back.\n\nWhat do you do?\n"}, "idempotency_key": "amw8gtiazcaiqib:narr"}
